Physical behaviors most likely to invalidate simplified assumptions
Slosh-induced side-load
1D model underestimates lateral effects.
Trapped air migration
Model may assume fixed air volume; real air moves.
Rod/bushing wear or swelling
Friction may change during run.
Pump vibration or tubing pull
Pump may mechanically influence motion.
Partial-fill metastability
Discrete state machine may hide continuous ambiguous states.
Rebound corruption
Endpoint impacts may alter fill/valve state.
Asymmetric flooding
Real inflow may tilt drum even when scalar fill rate looks adequate.
